```python
def _localname(tag): return tag.rsplit('}',1)[-1].lower()
def parse_jats_abstract(path):
    try:
        root = ET.parse(path).getroot()
    except ET.ParseError:
        return _regex_abstract(path)
    abs_nodes = [e for e in root.iter() if _localname(e.tag)=='abstract']
    if not abs_nodes: fallback regex
    texts=[]
    for a in abs_nodes:
        # skip graphical
        if a.attrib.get('abstract-type') in ('graphical','teaser'): continue
        # prefer text via itertext but avoid title? include
        chunks=[t.strip() for t in a.itertext() if t.strip()]
        texts.append(' '.join(chunks))
    return ' '.join(texts).strip()
```
itertext includes title labels "ABSTRACT" and section headings. Clean leading "ABSTRACT"/"Abstract". Fine; not critical. Could remove node tags title? better extract paragraphs only:
- Collect elements whose localname in {'p','title'}? We want content. Use itertext on abstract excluding nested `<title>`? Abstract title often "ABSTRACT" or "Summary". Section titles like "CONTEXT:" are informative but noise. Keep paragraphs only if present, else all text.
```
paras=[' '.join(e.itertext()) for e in a.iter() if localname(e.tag)=='p']
body=' '.join(paras) if paras else ' '.join(a.itertext())
```
Good.

