`document_features`:
```python
def build_features(title, abstract, text, encoder, include_fulltext=True, include_aux=False, ...):
    ta = (title + "\n\n" + abstract).strip() or title or abstract
    ta_vec = encoder.encode_texts([ta])[0]
    if include_fulltext and text.strip():
        chunks=chunk_text(...)
        if chunks:
            embs=encoder.encode_texts(chunks)
            mean=embs.mean(0); max=embs.max(0)
        ...
    else zeros
    feats=[ta_vec, mean, max] + aux
```
If no text but include_fulltext true → zeros. `full_text_available` computed from text.

Batch function: encode title+abstract in batch and chunk text in batches for efficiency. `document_features_batch(records, encoder, ...)`:
- Collect ta texts for all, encode in batches; collect all chunks with doc index; encode all chunks once; then aggregate. This is much faster.
